# Repo-root .dockerignore — applies when build context is `.`. TWO images build that way: the
# frontend prod Dockerfile, whose `build` stage COPYs frontend/ sources (tsconfig.json,
# vite.config.ts, index.html, public/, src/) — context stays repo root for that, including the
# Caddy config baked in from frontend/caddy/ — and sandbox-runner/agent-sandbox/Dockerfile, which
# needs the repo-root `contract/` directory alongside its own directory's script files.
# compile-service used to build from repo root too; it now builds elsewhere with its own
# .dockerignore, so it no longer applies here.

# The must-not-publish denylist. The root-context images are OPEN images
# and must carry only what the public export carries, so every `delete` row of
# scripts/lib/export-denylist.txt is excluded here too. `scripts/check-open-boundary.sh` rule 3
# asserts that every row is covered by a line in this file (the row itself, or a broader prefix such
# as `.github/` below), so this block is a gate rather than a convention. Keep it in the same order
# as the declaration. It is also what forced compile-service's context out of `.`: from here every
# one of its COPY sources is ignored.
#
# It is ONE line now because the denylist is one `delete` row. Every other denied path was
# relocated into that build's own directory, and the nineteen lines that used to sit here went
# with them.
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A LINE BACK: the rule-3 assertion is one-directional — denylist row ->
# .dockerignore coverage, NEVER the reverse (that is why the earlier Caddyfile.prod lines could
# linger here harmlessly for a long time). So an over-broad line in this block excludes OPEN source
# from the backend and frontend build contexts and EVERY GATE STAYS GREEN. The two that were live
# traps here were `classifiers/` (the framework/tool_error/metric_drift/data_gen half stays
# public) and `.claude/` (launch.json stays public); both are gone from here for that reason.
tessary-paid/

# Build artifacts
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python virtualenvs and tool caches. These are NOT covered by any denylist row and never were —
# previously they rode in on the blanket `classifiers/` line, which is gone because the open half
# of that tree publishes. `classifiers/.venv` is 1.3 GB on a machine that has run the tree's own
# documented `cd classifiers && uv sync`, and the frontend image builds from the repo root
# (docker-compose.yml `context: .`), so without these lines every `docker compose build frontend`
# uploads it to the daemon. The other build's own .dockerignore carries the same three globs for
# the same reason (compile-service/.venv alone is 229 MB).
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# VCS + editor
.git/
.github/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/

# Logs
**/*.log
hs_err_pid*.log

# Local env (never bake into images)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Compose files (not needed inside images)
docker-compose*.yml

# Python bytecode, and the open classifier tree's gitignored run outputs. These were listed one
# glob at a time originally, then rode in on the blanket `classifiers/` line, which was removed
# because the framework/tool_error/metric_drift/data_gen half publishes. The paths below mirror
# classifiers/.gitignore; the other build's own .dockerignore restates the experiments/ globs for
# the half that moved elsewhere.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
classifiers/**/data/
classifiers/**/artifacts/
classifiers/**/checkpoints/
classifiers/**/out/

# Misc
.DS_Store
caddy_data/
caddy_config/
